/-!
# Integral morphisms as directed limits of finite morphisms

An integral morphism of schemes with affine target is a directed inverse limit of finite
morphisms to the same target, and the stages may moreover be taken to be of finite presentation.
On an affine target `Spec A` the source is `Spec B` for an integral `A`-algebra `B`, and two
inverse systems are built.

* The system of subalgebras of `B` generated by the finite subsets of `B`: these are directed,
  their supremum is all of `B`, and each is a finite `A`-module. This gives finite stages with
  closed-immersion transition maps.
* The system of quotients `A[X_x : x ∈ s] ⧸ (relations)`, indexed by a finite set `s` of
  elements of `B` together with a finite set of polynomial relations between them which hold in
  `B`, where the relation ideal always contains one monic relation per generator. Each such
  quotient is a finite `A`-module *and* of finite presentation over `A`, and the colimit is
  again `B` because an arbitrary relation holding in `B` is imposed at some later stage.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.IntegralLimitPresentation` packages a directed inverse system of
  schemes over a fixed base, its structure morphisms to the base, and a limiting cone from the
  source, together with the assertion that every stage is finite over the base.
* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.FinitePresentationLimitPresentation` is such a presentation whose
  stages are in addition locally of finite presentation over the base.
* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.FinitePresentationStage` is the index of the second system above.

## Main results

* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.IntegralLimitPresentation.ofIso` and
  `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.FinitePresentationLimitPresentation.ofIso` transport a presentation
  along isomorphisms of the source and of the target.
* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.integralLimitPresentation` constructs a presentation with finite
  stages for any integral morphism with affine target.
* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.finitePresentationLimitPresentation` constructs a presentation whose
  stages are finite and of finite presentation, again for an affine target.

## Implementation notes

The inverse system is indexed by the opposite of a directed preorder, so that the diagram is a
functor out of `indexTypeᵒᵖ` and its limit is a plain limit of schemes rather than a limit in a
slice category. The finiteness of each stage is kept as a field returning `IsFinite`, which is a
class, so that it can be installed as a local instance at a stage.

The construction over an affine base is obtained by applying `Spec` to the colimit of the
diagram of finite subalgebras: `Spec` is a right adjoint, hence preserves limits, and a colimit
of rings is a limit in the opposite category.

Finite presentation of a morphism is recorded as `LocallyOfFinitePresentation`, which Mathlib
does not combine with quasi-compactness and quasi-separatedness into a single class; for a
finite morphism those two are automatic, so a stage of a `FinitePresentationLimitPresentation`
is of finite presentation in the full sense. This is
`FinitePresentationLimitPresentation.stageQuasiCompact` and
`FinitePresentationLimitPresentation.stageQuasiSeparated`.

The transition maps of the finitely presented system are not injective — a stage is a quotient
of a polynomial ring rather than a subalgebra of `B` — so the colimit cannot be computed as a
union. It is computed from the universal property directly: a cocone leg is determined on the
image of a variable, two stages agree there after passing to a common refinement
(`finitePresentationLeg_X`, `finitePresentationLeg_C`), and the ring-hom laws for the induced
map out of `B` are each read off from a single stage carrying the corresponding relation.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 09YZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09YZ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0817](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0817)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 086N](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/086N)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits
open AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

namespace Stacks.EtaleCohomology

/-- A presentation of a morphism of schemes as the limit of a directed inverse system of
morphisms that are finite over the same base. -/
structure IntegralLimitPresentation {X S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S) where
  /-- The directed preorder indexing the inverse system. -/
  indexType : Type u
  /-- The order on the index type. -/
  [indexPreorder : Preorder indexType]
  /-- The index type is nonempty. -/
  [indexNonempty : Nonempty indexType]
  /-- The index type is directed. -/
  [indexDirected : IsDirected indexType (· ≤ ·)]
  /-- The inverse system of schemes. -/
  diagram : indexTypeᵒᵖ ⥤ Scheme.{u}
  /-- The compatible structure morphisms from the stages to the base. -/
  structureMap : diagram ⟶ (Functor.const indexTypeᵒᵖ).obj S
  /-- The cone from the source scheme to the inverse system. -/
  limitCone : (Functor.const indexTypeᵒᵖ).obj X ⟶ diagram
  /-- Every map from the source through a stage induces the original morphism to the base. -/
  compatible : ∀ i, f = limitCone.app i ≫ structureMap.app i
  /-- The displayed cone exhibits the source as the limit of the inverse system. -/
  isLimit : IsLimit (Cone.mk X limitCone)
  /-- Every stage is finite over the base. -/
  stageFinite : ∀ i, IsFinite (structureMap.app i)

namespace IntegralLimitPresentation

/-- Transport a limit presentation along an isomorphism of the source and an isomorphism of the
target. -/
def ofIso {X S X' S' : Scheme.{u}} {f : X ⟶ S} {f' : X' ⟶ S'}
    (p : IntegralLimitPresentation f') (e : X ≅ X') (d : S ≅ S')
    (h : f ≫ d.hom = e.hom ≫ f') : IntegralLimitPresentation f :=
  letI := p.indexPreorder
  letI := p.indexNonempty
  letI := p.indexDirected
  { indexType := p.indexType
    diagram := p.diagram
    structureMap :=
      { app := fun i => p.structureMap.app i ≫ d.inv
        naturality := fun i j g => by simp }
    limitCone :=
      { app := fun i => e.hom ≫ p.limitCone.app i
        naturality := fun i j g => by
          have hn : p.limitCone.app j = p.limitCone.app i ≫ p.diagram.map g := by
            simpa using p.limitCone.naturality g
          simpa using e.hom ≫= hn }
    compatible := fun i => by
      calc f = (f ≫ d.hom) ≫ d.inv := by simp
        _ = (e.hom ≫ f') ≫ d.inv := by rw [h]
        _ = (e.hom ≫ p.limitCone.app i ≫ p.structureMap.app i) ≫ d.inv := by rw [← p.compatible i]
        _ = (e.hom ≫ p.limitCone.app i) ≫ p.structureMap.app i ≫ d.inv := by
            simp [Category.assoc]
    isLimit :=
      p.isLimit.ofIsoLimit (Cone.ext e.symm (fun j => by simp))
    stageFinite := fun i => by
      have := p.stageFinite i
      infer_instance }

end IntegralLimitPresentation

/-- A presentation of a morphism of schemes as the limit of a directed inverse system of
morphisms that are finite and locally of finite presentation over the same base.

This is the shape of the conclusion of [Stacks, Tag 09YZ]: the stages are finite and of finite
presentation over the base. Quasi-compactness and quasi-separatedness of a stage over the base
are automatic from finiteness, see `stageQuasiCompact` and `stageQuasiSeparated`, so a stage is
of finite presentation in the full sense. -/
structure FinitePresentationLimitPresentation {X S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S) where
  /-- The directed preorder indexing the inverse system. -/
  indexType : Type u
  /-- The order on the index type. -/
  [indexPreorder : Preorder indexType]
  /-- The index type is nonempty. -/
  [indexNonempty : Nonempty indexType]
  /-- The index type is directed. -/
  [indexDirected : IsDirected indexType (· ≤ ·)]
  /-- The inverse system of schemes. -/
  diagram : indexTypeᵒᵖ ⥤ Scheme.{u}
  /-- The compatible structure morphisms from the stages to the base. -/
  structureMap : diagram ⟶ (Functor.const indexTypeᵒᵖ).obj S
  /-- The cone from the source scheme to the inverse system. -/
  limitCone : (Functor.const indexTypeᵒᵖ).obj X ⟶ diagram
  /-- Every map from the source through a stage induces the original morphism to the base. -/
  compatible : ∀ i, f = limitCone.app i ≫ structureMap.app i
  /-- The displayed cone exhibits the source as the limit of the inverse system. -/
  isLimit : IsLimit (Cone.mk X limitCone)
  /-- Every stage is finite over the base. -/
  stageFinite : ∀ i, IsFinite (structureMap.app i)
  /-- Every stage is locally of finite presentation over the base. -/
  stageLocallyOfFinitePresentation : ∀ i, LocallyOfFinitePresentation (structureMap.app i)

namespace FinitePresentationLimitPresentation

variable {X S : Scheme.{u}} {f : X ⟶ S}

/-- Forget the finite presentation of the stages. -/
def toIntegralLimitPresentation (p : FinitePresentationLimitPresentation f) :
    IntegralLimitPresentation f :=
  letI := p.indexPreorder
  letI := p.indexNonempty
  letI := p.indexDirected
  { indexType := p.indexType
    diagram := p.diagram
    structureMap := p.structureMap
    limitCone := p.limitCone
    compatible := p.compatible
    isLimit := p.isLimit
    stageFinite := p.stageFinite }

/-- Each stage of such a presentation is quasi-compact over the base, being finite. -/
lemma stageQuasiCompact (p : FinitePresentationLimitPresentation f) :
    letI := p.indexPreorder
    ∀ i, QuasiCompact (p.structureMap.app i) :=
  let := p.indexPreorder
  fun i =>
    let := p.stageFinite i
    inferInstance

/-- Each stage of such a presentation is quasi-separated over the base, being finite. -/
lemma stageQuasiSeparated (p : FinitePresentationLimitPresentation f) :
    letI := p.indexPreorder
    ∀ i, QuasiSeparated (p.structureMap.app i) :=
  let := p.indexPreorder
  fun i =>
    let := p.stageFinite i
    inferInstance

/-- Transport a presentation by finite morphisms of finite presentation along an isomorphism of
the source and an isomorphism of the target. -/
def ofIso {X' S' : Scheme.{u}} {f' : X' ⟶ S'}
    (p : FinitePresentationLimitPresentation f') (e : X ≅ X') (d : S ≅ S')
    (h : f ≫ d.hom = e.hom ≫ f') : FinitePresentationLimitPresentation f :=
  letI := p.indexPreorder
  letI := p.indexNonempty
  letI := p.indexDirected
  { indexType := p.indexType
    diagram := p.diagram
    structureMap :=
      { app := fun i => p.structureMap.app i ≫ d.inv
        naturality := fun i j g => by simp }
    limitCone :=
      { app := fun i => e.hom ≫ p.limitCone.app i
        naturality := fun i j g => by
          have hn : p.limitCone.app j = p.limitCone.app i ≫ p.diagram.map g := by
            simpa using p.limitCone.naturality g
          simpa using e.hom ≫= hn }
    compatible := fun i => by
      calc f = (f ≫ d.hom) ≫ d.inv := by simp
        _ = (e.hom ≫ f') ≫ d.inv := by rw [h]
        _ = (e.hom ≫ p.limitCone.app i ≫ p.structureMap.app i) ≫ d.inv := by rw [← p.compatible i]
        _ = (e.hom ≫ p.limitCone.app i) ≫ p.structureMap.app i ≫ d.inv := by
            simp [Category.assoc]
    isLimit :=
      p.isLimit.ofIsoLimit (Cone.ext e.symm (fun j => by simp))
    stageFinite := fun i => by
      have := p.stageFinite i
      infer_instance
    stageLocallyOfFinitePresentation := fun i => by
      have := p.stageLocallyOfFinitePresentation i
      infer_instance }

end FinitePresentationLimitPresentation

section Affine

variable (A B : Type u) [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]

/-- The inverse system of the `A`-subalgebras of `B` generated by the finite subsets of `B`,
as a diagram of commutative rings indexed by `Finset B`. -/
def finsetSubalgebraDiagram : Finset B ⥤ CommRingCat.{u} where
  obj s := CommRingCat.of (Algebra.adjoin A (s : Set B))
  map {s t} h := CommRingCat.ofHom
    (Subalgebra.inclusion (Algebra.adjoin_mono (Finset.coe_subset.mpr (leOfHom h)))).toRingHom
  map_id s := by ext x; rfl
  map_comp f g := by ext x; rfl

/-- The cocone on `finsetSubalgebraDiagram` given by the inclusions of the subalgebras into `B`. -/
def finsetSubalgebraCocone : Cocone (finsetSubalgebraDiagram A B) where
  pt := CommRingCat.of B
  ι :=
    { app := fun s => CommRingCat.ofHom (Algebra.adjoin A (s : Set B)).val.toRingHom
      naturality := fun s t h => by ext x; rfl }

variable {A B}

/-- A leg of a cocone on `finsetSubalgebraDiagram`, with its domain spelled as the subalgebra
rather than as a value of the diagram. -/
def finsetCoconeLeg (T : Cocone (finsetSubalgebraDiagram A B)) (s : Finset B) :
    Algebra.adjoin A (s : Set B) →+* T.pt :=
  (T.ι.app s).hom

/-- The leg at a larger stage, precomposed with the inclusion of subalgebras, is the leg at the
smaller stage. -/
lemma finsetCoconeLeg_comp_inclusion (T : Cocone (finsetSubalgebraDiagram A B)) {s t : Finset B}
    (h : s ≤ t) (x : Algebra.adjoin A (s : Set B)) :
    finsetCoconeLeg T t (Subalgebra.inclusion
        (Algebra.adjoin_mono (Finset.coe_subset.mpr h)) x) = finsetCoconeLeg T s x :=
  congrArg (fun φ : (finsetSubalgebraDiagram A B).obj s ⟶ T.pt => φ.hom x)
    (T.ι.naturality (homOfLE h))

/-- Two stages of `finsetSubalgebraDiagram` containing the same element of `B` send it to the same
element of the vertex of any cocone. -/
lemma finsetCoconeLeg_agree (T : Cocone (finsetSubalgebraDiagram A B))
    (s t : Finset B) (x : B) (hs : x ∈ Algebra.adjoin A (s : Set B))
    (ht : x ∈ Algebra.adjoin A (t : Set B)) :
    finsetCoconeLeg T s ⟨x, hs⟩ = finsetCoconeLeg T t ⟨x, ht⟩ := by
  classical
  have hsu : s ≤ s ∪ t := Finset.subset_union_left
  have htu : t ≤ s ∪ t := Finset.subset_union_right
  rw [← finsetCoconeLeg_comp_inclusion T hsu ⟨x, hs⟩,
    ← finsetCoconeLeg_comp_inclusion T htu ⟨x, ht⟩]
  rfl

/-- The map out of `B` determined by a cocone on `finsetSubalgebraDiagram`: an element of `B` is
sent through the stage it generates. -/
def finsetCoconeDesc (T : Cocone (finsetSubalgebraDiagram A B)) : B →+* T.pt where
  toFun b := finsetCoconeLeg T {b} ⟨b, Algebra.subset_adjoin (by simp)⟩
  map_one' := by
    have : finsetCoconeLeg T ({1} : Finset B) ⟨1, Algebra.subset_adjoin (by simp)⟩ =
        finsetCoconeLeg T ({1} : Finset B) 1 := by
      congr 1
    rw [this, map_one]
  map_zero' := by
    have : finsetCoconeLeg T ({0} : Finset B) ⟨0, Algebra.subset_adjoin (by simp)⟩ =
        finsetCoconeLeg T ({0} : Finset B) 0 := by
      congr 1
    rw [this, map_zero]
  map_mul' a b := by
    classical
    have ha : a ∈ Algebra.adjoin A (({a, b} : Finset B) : Set B) :=
      Algebra.subset_adjoin (by simp)
    have hb : b ∈ Algebra.adjoin A (({a, b} : Finset B) : Set B) :=
      Algebra.subset_adjoin (by simp)
    have hab : a * b ∈ Algebra.adjoin A (({a, b} : Finset B) : Set B) := mul_mem ha hb
    rw [finsetCoconeLeg_agree T _ ({a, b} : Finset B) (a * b) _ hab,
      finsetCoconeLeg_agree T _ ({a, b} : Finset B) a _ ha,
      finsetCoconeLeg_agree T _ ({a, b} : Finset B) b _ hb]
    have : (⟨a * b, hab⟩ : Algebra.adjoin A (({a, b} : Finset B) : Set B)) =
        ⟨a, ha⟩ * ⟨b, hb⟩ := rfl
    rw [this, map_mul]
  map_add' a b := by
    classical
    have ha : a ∈ Algebra.adjoin A (({a, b} : Finset B) : Set B) :=
      Algebra.subset_adjoin (by simp)
    have hb : b ∈ Algebra.adjoin A (({a, b} : Finset B) : Set B) :=
      Algebra.subset_adjoin (by simp)
    have hab : a + b ∈ Algebra.adjoin A (({a, b} : Finset B) : Set B) := add_mem ha hb
    rw [finsetCoconeLeg_agree T _ ({a, b} : Finset B) (a + b) _ hab,
      finsetCoconeLeg_agree T _ ({a, b} : Finset B) a _ ha,
      finsetCoconeLeg_agree T _ ({a, b} : Finset B) b _ hb]
    have : (⟨a + b, hab⟩ : Algebra.adjoin A (({a, b} : Finset B) : Set B)) =
        ⟨a, ha⟩ + ⟨b, hb⟩ := rfl
    rw [this, map_add]

/-- On an element of a stage, `finsetCoconeDesc` agrees with the leg at that stage. -/
lemma finsetCoconeDesc_apply_coe (T : Cocone (finsetSubalgebraDiagram A B)) (s : Finset B)
    (x : Algebra.adjoin A (s : Set B)) :
    finsetCoconeDesc T (x : B) = finsetCoconeLeg T s x :=
  finsetCoconeLeg_agree T _ s (x : B) _ x.2

/-- Any ring map out of `B` compatible with the inclusions of the subalgebras generated by
finite subsets agrees with `finsetCoconeDesc`. -/
lemma finsetCoconeDesc_unique (T : Cocone (finsetSubalgebraDiagram A B))
    (m : (finsetSubalgebraCocone A B).pt ⟶ T.pt)
    (hm : ∀ s, (finsetSubalgebraCocone A B).ι.app s ≫ m = T.ι.app s) (b : B) :
    m.hom b = finsetCoconeDesc T b := by
  have hx : b ∈ Algebra.adjoin A (({b} : Finset B) : Set B) :=
    Algebra.subset_adjoin (by simp)
  rw [finsetCoconeDesc_apply_coe T ({b} : Finset B) ⟨b, hx⟩]
  exact congrArg
    (fun φ : (finsetSubalgebraDiagram A B).obj ({b} : Finset B) ⟶ T.pt => φ.hom ⟨b, hx⟩)
    (hm ({b} : Finset B))

/-- The inclusions of the subalgebras generated by finite subsets exhibit `B` as the colimit of
`finsetSubalgebraDiagram`. -/
def finsetSubalgebraIsColimit : IsColimit (finsetSubalgebraCocone A B) where
  desc T := CommRingCat.ofHom (finsetCoconeDesc T)
  fac T s := by
    ext x
    exact finsetCoconeDesc_apply_coe T s x
  uniq T m hm := by
    ext b
    exact finsetCoconeDesc_unique T m hm b

variable (A B)

/-- The structure morphisms of the inverse system of spectra of the subalgebras to `Spec A`. -/
noncomputable def finsetSubalgebraSpecStructureMap :
    (finsetSubalgebraDiagram A B).op ⋙ Scheme.Spec ⟶
      (Functor.const (Finset B)ᵒᵖ).obj (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)) where
  app s := Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
    (algebraMap A (Algebra.adjoin A ((s.unop : Finset B) : Set B))))
  naturality s t h := by
    have key : CommRingCat.ofHom
          (algebraMap A (Algebra.adjoin A ((t.unop : Finset B) : Set B))) ≫
        (finsetSubalgebraDiagram A B).map h.unop =
      CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A (Algebra.adjoin A ((s.unop : Finset B) : Set B))) := by
      ext a; rfl
    change Spec.map ((finsetSubalgebraDiagram A B).map h.unop) ≫
        Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
          (algebraMap A (Algebra.adjoin A ((t.unop : Finset B) : Set B)))) =
      Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
        (algebraMap A (Algebra.adjoin A ((s.unop : Finset B) : Set B)))) ≫ 𝟙 _
    rw [Category.comp_id]
    exact (Spec.map_comp _ _).symm.trans (congrArg Spec.map key)

/-- The legs of the image under `Spec` of `finsetSubalgebraCocone` are the spectra of the
inclusions of the subalgebras. -/
lemma finsetSubalgebraSpecCone_π_app (s : (Finset B)ᵒᵖ) :
    (Scheme.Spec.mapCone (finsetSubalgebraCocone A B).op).π.app s =
      Spec.map ((finsetSubalgebraCocone A B).ι.app s.unop) := rfl

/-- For an integral algebra `B` over `A`, the spectrum
of `B` is the directed inverse limit of the spectra of the subalgebras of `B` generated by the
finite subsets of `B`, each of which is finite over `Spec A`. -/
noncomputable def integralLimitPresentationSpec [Algebra.IsIntegral A B] :
    IntegralLimitPresentation (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))) where
  indexType := Finset B
  diagram := (finsetSubalgebraDiagram A B).op ⋙ Scheme.Spec
  structureMap := finsetSubalgebraSpecStructureMap A B
  limitCone := (Scheme.Spec.mapCone (finsetSubalgebraCocone A B).op).π
  compatible s := by
    have key : CommRingCat.ofHom
          (algebraMap A (Algebra.adjoin A ((s.unop : Finset B) : Set B))) ≫
        (finsetSubalgebraCocone A B).ι.app s.unop =
      CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B) := by
      ext a; rfl
    change Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B)) =
      Spec.map ((finsetSubalgebraCocone A B).ι.app s.unop) ≫
        Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
          (algebraMap A (Algebra.adjoin A ((s.unop : Finset B) : Set B))))
    exact (congrArg Spec.map key).symm.trans (Spec.map_comp _ _)
  isLimit := isLimitOfPreserves Scheme.Spec (finsetSubalgebraIsColimit (A := A) (B := B)).op
  stageFinite s := by
    refine (AlgebraicGeometry.IsFinite.SpecMap_iff (CommRingCat.ofHom
      (algebraMap A (Algebra.adjoin A ((s.unop : Finset B) : Set B))))).mpr ?_
    exact RingHom.finite_algebraMap.mpr
      (Stacks.RingTheory.IntegralApproximation.moduleFinite_adjoin_finset _)

end Affine

section AffineFinitePresentation

/-! ### Inclusions of finite sets -/

section Inclusion

variable {B : Type u}

/-- The map of subtypes induced by an inclusion of finite sets. -/
def finsetInclusion {s t : Finset B} (h : s ⊆ t) (x : {x : B // x ∈ s}) : {x : B // x ∈ t} :=
  ⟨x.1, h x.2⟩

/-- The map induced by the inclusion of a finite set into itself is the identity. -/
@[simp]
lemma finsetInclusion_self {s : Finset B} (h : s ⊆ s) : finsetInclusion h = id := rfl

/-- The maps induced by inclusions of finite sets compose to the map induced by the composite
inclusion. -/
lemma finsetInclusion_comp {s t v : Finset B} (h : s ⊆ t) (h' : t ⊆ v) :
    finsetInclusion h' ∘ finsetInclusion h = finsetInclusion (h.trans h') := rfl

/-- The map induced by an inclusion of finite sets commutes with the coercions to `B`. -/
@[simp]
lemma coe_comp_finsetInclusion {s t : Finset B} (h : s ⊆ t) :
    (fun x : {x : B // x ∈ t} => (x : B)) ∘ finsetInclusion h =
      fun x : {x : B // x ∈ s} => (x : B) := rfl

/-- The map induced by an inclusion of finite sets does not change the underlying element. -/
@[simp]
lemma coe_finsetInclusion {s t : Finset B} (h : s ⊆ t) (x : {x : B // x ∈ s}) :
    (finsetInclusion h x : B) = (x : B) := rfl

end Inclusion

/-! ### A chosen monic annihilating polynomial -/

variable (A B : Type u) [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]

/-- Every element of an integral algebra is annihilated by a monic polynomial over the base. -/
lemma exists_monic_aeval_eq_zero [Algebra.IsIntegral A B] (b : B) :
    ∃ p : Polynomial A, p.Monic ∧ Polynomial.aeval b p = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨p, hp, hp0⟩ := Algebra.IsIntegral.isIntegral (R := A) b
  exact ⟨p, hp, by simpa [Polynomial.aeval_def] using hp0⟩

variable [Algebra.IsIntegral A B]

/-- A chosen monic polynomial over `A` annihilating a given element of the integral algebra `B`. -/
noncomputable def integralPoly (b : B) : Polynomial A :=
  (exists_monic_aeval_eq_zero A B b).choose

/-- The chosen annihilating polynomial is monic. -/
lemma integralPoly_monic (b : B) : (integralPoly A B b).Monic :=
  (exists_monic_aeval_eq_zero A B b).choose_spec.1

/-- The chosen annihilating polynomial annihilates the element it was chosen for. -/
lemma aeval_integralPoly (b : B) : Polynomial.aeval b (integralPoly A B b) = 0 :=
  (exists_monic_aeval_eq_zero A B b).choose_spec.2

/-! ### The index of the finitely presented system -/

/-- An index for the system of finite, finitely presented approximations of the integral
`A`-algebra `B`: a finite set of elements of `B`, to be used as generators, together with a
finite set of polynomial relations between them which hold in `B`, to be imposed.

The associated algebra is the polynomial algebra on the generators modulo the imposed relations
*and* one monic relation per generator, which is what makes it module-finite over `A`. -/
structure FinitePresentationStage where
  /-- The chosen finite set of generators. -/
  gens : Finset B
  /-- The chosen finite set of imposed relations. -/
  rels : Finset (MvPolynomial {x : B // x ∈ gens} A)
  /-- Every imposed relation holds in `B`. -/
  rels_mem_ker : ∀ r ∈ rels, MvPolynomial.aeval (fun x : {x : B // x ∈ gens} => (x : B)) r = 0

namespace FinitePresentationStage

variable {A B}

/-- Evaluation of the polynomial algebra on the generators of a stage at those generators. -/
noncomputable def evalHom (i : FinitePresentationStage A B) :
    MvPolynomial {x : B // x ∈ i.gens} A →ₐ[A] B :=
  MvPolynomial.aeval fun x => (x : B)

omit [Algebra.IsIntegral A B] in
/-- `evalHom` sends a variable to the corresponding generator. -/
@[simp]
lemma evalHom_X (i : FinitePresentationStage A B) (x : {x : B // x ∈ i.gens}) :
    i.evalHom (MvPolynomial.X x) = (x : B) := by
  simp [evalHom]

omit [Algebra.IsIntegral A B] in
/-- `evalHom` sends a constant to its image under `algebraMap A B`. -/
@[simp]
lemma evalHom_C (i : FinitePresentationStage A B) (a : A) :
    i.evalHom (MvPolynomial.C a) = algebraMap A B a := by
  simp [evalHom]

/-- The monic relation imposed on a generator by its integrality over `A`. -/
noncomputable def monicRel (i : FinitePresentationStage A B)
    (x : {x : B // x ∈ i.gens}) : MvPolynomial {x : B // x ∈ i.gens} A :=
  Polynomial.aeval (MvPolynomial.X x) (integralPoly A B (x : B))

/-- The relation ideal of a stage: the imposed relations together with one monic relation for
each generator. -/
noncomputable def rel (i : FinitePresentationStage A B) :
    Ideal (MvPolynomial {x : B // x ∈ i.gens} A) :=
  Ideal.span ((i.rels : Set (MvPolynomial {x : B // x ∈ i.gens} A)) ∪ Set.range i.monicRel)

/-- The algebra presented by a stage. -/
abbrev ring (i : FinitePresentationStage A B) : Type u :=
  MvPolynomial {x : B // x ∈ i.gens} A ⧸ i.rel

/-- The relation ideal of a stage is finitely generated. -/
lemma rel_fg (i : FinitePresentationStage A B) : i.rel.FG :=
  Submodule.fg_span (i.rels.finite_toSet.union (Set.finite_range _))

/-- An imposed relation lies in the relation ideal. -/
lemma rels_le_rel (i : FinitePresentationStage A B) {r : MvPolynomial {x : B // x ∈ i.gens} A}
    (hr : r ∈ i.rels) : r ∈ i.rel :=
  Ideal.subset_span (Or.inl (by simpa using hr))

/-- A monic relation lies in the relation ideal. -/
lemma monicRel_mem_rel (i : FinitePresentationStage A B) (x : {x : B // x ∈ i.gens}) :
    i.monicRel x ∈ i.rel :=
  Ideal.subset_span (Or.inr ⟨x, rfl⟩)

/-- The monic relation on a generator holds in `B`. -/
lemma evalHom_monicRel (i : FinitePresentationStage A B) (x : {x : B // x ∈ i.gens}) :
    i.evalHom (i.monicRel x) = 0 := by
  rw [monicRel, ← Polynomial.aeval_algHom_apply, evalHom_X, aeval_integralPoly]

/-- Every element of the relation ideal of a stage vanishes in `B`. -/
lemma rel_le_ker (i : FinitePresentationStage A B) :
    i.rel ≤ RingHom.ker i.evalHom.toRingHom := by
  rw [rel, Ideal.span_le]
  rintro r (hr | ⟨x, rfl⟩)
  · exact RingHom.mem_ker.mpr (i.rels_mem_ker r (by simpa using hr))
  · exact RingHom.mem_ker.mpr (i.evalHom_monicRel x)

/-- The map from the algebra presented by a stage to `B`. -/
noncomputable def toB (i : FinitePresentationStage A B) : i.ring →ₐ[A] B :=
  Ideal.Quotient.liftₐ i.rel i.evalHom fun _ ha => i.rel_le_ker ha

/-- `toB` sends the class of a polynomial to its evaluation at the generators. -/
@[simp]
lemma toB_mk (i : FinitePresentationStage A B) (w : MvPolynomial {x : B // x ∈ i.gens} A) :
    i.toB (Ideal.Quotient.mk i.rel w) = i.evalHom w := rfl

/-- The algebra presented by a stage is a finite `A`-module: it is generated as an `A`-algebra by
the images of the variables, and each of these is integral because the corresponding monic
relation is imposed. -/
lemma moduleFinite (i : FinitePresentationStage A B) : Module.Finite A i.ring := by
  have hint : ∀ x : {x : B // x ∈ i.gens},
      IsIntegral A ((Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ A i.rel) (MvPolynomial.X x)) := by
    intro x
    refine ⟨integralPoly A B (x : B), integralPoly_monic A B _, ?_⟩
    rw [← Polynomial.aeval_def, Polynomial.aeval_algHom_apply]
    exact Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.2 (i.monicRel_mem_rel x)
  have htop : Algebra.adjoin A
      (Set.range fun x => (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ A i.rel) (MvPolynomial.X x)) = ⊤ := by
    have h := AlgHom.map_adjoin (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ A i.rel)
      (Set.range (MvPolynomial.X : {x : B // x ∈ i.gens} → MvPolynomial _ A))
    rw [MvPolynomial.adjoin_range_X, Algebra.map_top] at h
    simp only [← Set.range_comp, Function.comp_def] at h
    rw [← h, AlgHom.range_eq_top]
    exact Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ_surjective A i.rel
  have hfin : Module.Finite A (Algebra.adjoin A
      (Set.range fun x => (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ A i.rel) (MvPolynomial.X x))) :=
    Algebra.finite_adjoin_of_finite_of_isIntegral (Set.finite_range _) <| by
      rintro _ ⟨x, rfl⟩
      exact hint x
  rw [htop] at hfin
  exact Module.Finite.equiv (Subalgebra.topEquiv (R := A) (A := i.ring)).toLinearEquiv

/-- The algebra presented by a stage is of finite presentation over `A`: it is a polynomial
algebra in finitely many variables modulo a finitely generated ideal. -/
lemma finitePresentation (i : FinitePresentationStage A B) :
    Algebra.FinitePresentation A i.ring :=
  Algebra.FinitePresentation.quotient i.rel_fg

/-- The order on stages: more generators, and every imposed relation stays imposed. -/
protected def LE (i j : FinitePresentationStage A B) : Prop :=
  i.gens ⊆ j.gens ∧
    ∀ (h : i.gens ⊆ j.gens) (r : MvPolynomial {x : B // x ∈ i.gens} A), r ∈ i.rels →
      MvPolynomial.rename (finsetInclusion h) r ∈ j.rels

/-- Stages are preordered by `FinitePresentationStage.LE`. -/
instance : Preorder (FinitePresentationStage A B) where
  le := FinitePresentationStage.LE
  le_refl i := ⟨subset_rfl, fun h r hr => by
    rwa [finsetInclusion_self, MvPolynomial.rename_id_apply]⟩
  le_trans i j k hij hjk := ⟨hij.1.trans hjk.1, fun h r hr => by
    have h2 := hjk.2 hjk.1 _ (hij.2 hij.1 r hr)
    rwa [MvPolynomial.rename_rename, finsetInclusion_comp] at h2⟩

/-- The stage with no generators and no relations. -/
instance : Nonempty (FinitePresentationStage A B) := ⟨⟨∅, ∅, by simp⟩⟩

/-- Any two stages lie below the stage on the union of their generators, imposing the renamed
relations of both. -/
instance : IsDirected (FinitePresentationStage A B) (· ≤ ·) := by
  classical
  refine ⟨fun i j => ?_⟩
  have hi : i.gens ⊆ i.gens ∪ j.gens := Finset.subset_union_left
  have hj : j.gens ⊆ i.gens ∪ j.gens := Finset.subset_union_right
  refine ⟨⟨i.gens ∪ j.gens,
    i.rels.image (MvPolynomial.rename (finsetInclusion hi)) ∪
      j.rels.image (MvPolynomial.rename (finsetInclusion hj)), ?_⟩,
    ⟨hi, fun h r hr => ?_⟩, ⟨hj, fun h r hr => ?_⟩⟩
  · intro r hr
    simp only [Finset.mem_union, Finset.mem_image] at hr
    obtain (⟨r', hr', rfl⟩ | ⟨r', hr', rfl⟩) := hr
    · rw [MvPolynomial.aeval_rename, coe_comp_finsetInclusion]
      exact i.rels_mem_ker r' hr'
    · rw [MvPolynomial.aeval_rename, coe_comp_finsetInclusion]
      exact j.rels_mem_ker r' hr'
  · exact Finset.mem_union_left _ (Finset.mem_image_of_mem _ hr)
  · exact Finset.mem_union_right _ (Finset.mem_image_of_mem _ hr)

/-- Renaming along an inclusion of stages carries a monic relation to a monic relation. -/
lemma rename_monicRel {i j : FinitePresentationStage A B} (h : i ≤ j)
    (x : {x : B // x ∈ i.gens}) :
    MvPolynomial.rename (finsetInclusion h.1) (i.monicRel x) =
      j.monicRel (finsetInclusion h.1 x) := by
  rw [monicRel, monicRel, ← Polynomial.aeval_algHom_apply, MvPolynomial.rename_X,
    coe_finsetInclusion]

/-- Renaming along an inclusion of stages carries the relation ideal into the relation ideal. -/
lemma rename_mem_rel {i j : FinitePresentationStage A B} (h : i ≤ j)
    {w : MvPolynomial {x : B // x ∈ i.gens} A} (hw : w ∈ i.rel) :
    MvPolynomial.rename (finsetInclusion h.1) w ∈ j.rel := by
  have hle : i.rel ≤ Ideal.comap
      (MvPolynomial.rename (finsetInclusion h.1)).toRingHom j.rel := by
    rw [rel, Ideal.span_le]
    rintro r (hr | ⟨x, rfl⟩)
    · exact Ideal.mem_comap.mpr (j.rels_le_rel (h.2 h.1 r (by simpa using hr)))
    · refine Ideal.mem_comap.mpr ?_
      rw [show (MvPolynomial.rename (finsetInclusion h.1)).toRingHom (i.monicRel x) =
        j.monicRel (finsetInclusion h.1 x) from rename_monicRel h x]
      exact j.monicRel_mem_rel _
  exact hle hw

/-- The transition map of the system of stage algebras. -/
noncomputable def map {i j : FinitePresentationStage A B} (h : i ≤ j) : i.ring →ₐ[A] j.ring :=
  Ideal.Quotient.liftₐ i.rel
    ((Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ A j.rel).comp (MvPolynomial.rename (finsetInclusion h.1)))
    fun _ ha => Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.2 (rename_mem_rel h ha)

/-- The transition map sends the class of a polynomial to the class of its renaming along the
inclusion of generators. -/
@[simp]
lemma map_mk {i j : FinitePresentationStage A B} (h : i ≤ j)
    (w : MvPolynomial {x : B // x ∈ i.gens} A) :
    map h (Ideal.Quotient.mk i.rel w) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk j.rel (MvPolynomial.rename (finsetInclusion h.1) w) := rfl

end FinitePresentationStage

/-- The system of finite, finitely presented approximations of the integral algebra `B`. -/
noncomputable def finitePresentationDiagram :
    FinitePresentationStage A B ⥤ CommRingCat.{u} where
  obj i := CommRingCat.of i.ring
  map h := CommRingCat.ofHom (FinitePresentationStage.map (leOfHom h)).toRingHom
  map_id i := by
    refine CommRingCat.hom_ext (RingHom.ext fun x => ?_)
    obtain ⟨w, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective x
    rw [CommRingCat.hom_ofHom]
    change Ideal.Quotient.mk i.rel (MvPolynomial.rename (finsetInclusion _) w) = _
    rw [finsetInclusion_self, MvPolynomial.rename_id_apply]
    rfl
  map_comp h h' := by
    refine CommRingCat.hom_ext (RingHom.ext fun x => ?_)
    obtain ⟨w, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective x
    rw [CommRingCat.hom_comp]
    change Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (MvPolynomial.rename (finsetInclusion _) w) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (MvPolynomial.rename (finsetInclusion _)
        (MvPolynomial.rename (finsetInclusion _) w))
    rw [MvPolynomial.rename_rename, finsetInclusion_comp]

/-- The cocone on `finitePresentationDiagram` given by evaluation at the generators. -/
noncomputable def finitePresentationCocone : Cocone (finitePresentationDiagram A B) where
  pt := CommRingCat.of B
  ι :=
    { app := fun i => CommRingCat.ofHom i.toB.toRingHom
      naturality := fun i j h => by
        refine CommRingCat.hom_ext (RingHom.ext fun x => ?_)
        obtain ⟨w, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective x
        change j.evalHom (MvPolynomial.rename (finsetInclusion _) w) = i.evalHom w
        rw [FinitePresentationStage.evalHom, FinitePresentationStage.evalHom,
          MvPolynomial.aeval_rename, coe_comp_finsetInclusion] }

variable {A B}

/-- A leg of a cocone on `finitePresentationDiagram`, with its domain spelled as the stage
algebra rather than as a value of the diagram. -/
noncomputable def finitePresentationLeg (T : Cocone (finitePresentationDiagram A B))
    (i : FinitePresentationStage A B) : i.ring →+* T.pt :=
  (T.ι.app i).hom

/-- Passing to a larger stage does not change the value of a cocone leg on a renamed
polynomial. -/
lemma finitePresentationLeg_rename (T : Cocone (finitePresentationDiagram A B))
    {i j : FinitePresentationStage A B} (h : i ≤ j)
    (w : MvPolynomial {x : B // x ∈ i.gens} A) :
    finitePresentationLeg T j
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk j.rel (MvPolynomial.rename (finsetInclusion h.1) w)) =
      finitePresentationLeg T i (Ideal.Quotient.mk i.rel w) :=
  congrArg
    (fun φ : (finitePresentationDiagram A B).obj i ⟶ T.pt =>
      φ.hom (Ideal.Quotient.mk i.rel w)) (T.ι.naturality (homOfLE h))

/-- Two cocone legs agree on classes of polynomials which become equal after renaming to any common
larger stage. -/
private lemma finitePresentationLeg_eq_of_rename (T : Cocone (finitePresentationDiagram A B))
    {i j : FinitePresentationStage A B} {v : MvPolynomial {x : B // x ∈ i.gens} A}
    {w : MvPolynomial {x : B // x ∈ j.gens} A}
    (h : ∀ (k : FinitePresentationStage A B) (hik : i ≤ k) (hjk : j ≤ k),
      MvPolynomial.rename (finsetInclusion hik.1) v =
        MvPolynomial.rename (finsetInclusion hjk.1) w) :
    finitePresentationLeg T i (Ideal.Quotient.mk i.rel v) =
      finitePresentationLeg T j (Ideal.Quotient.mk j.rel w) := by
  obtain ⟨k, hik, hjk⟩ : ∃ k, i ≤ k ∧ j ≤ k := directed_of (· ≤ ·) i j
  rw [← finitePresentationLeg_rename T hik, ← finitePresentationLeg_rename T hjk, h k hik hjk]

/-- All the legs of a cocone agree on the constants. -/
lemma finitePresentationLeg_C (T : Cocone (finitePresentationDiagram A B))
    (i j : FinitePresentationStage A B) (a : A) :
    finitePresentationLeg T i (Ideal.Quotient.mk i.rel (MvPolynomial.C a)) =
      finitePresentationLeg T j (Ideal.Quotient.mk j.rel (MvPolynomial.C a)) :=
  finitePresentationLeg_eq_of_rename T fun _ _ _ => by simp only [MvPolynomial.rename_C]

/-- All the legs of a cocone agree on the variable attached to a given element of `B`. -/
lemma finitePresentationLeg_X (T : Cocone (finitePresentationDiagram A B))
    {i j : FinitePresentationStage A B} {b : B} (hi : b ∈ i.gens) (hj : b ∈ j.gens) :
    finitePresentationLeg T i (Ideal.Quotient.mk i.rel (MvPolynomial.X ⟨b, hi⟩)) =
      finitePresentationLeg T j (Ideal.Quotient.mk j.rel (MvPolynomial.X ⟨b, hj⟩)) :=
  finitePresentationLeg_eq_of_rename T fun _ _ _ => by simp only [MvPolynomial.rename_X]; rfl

/-- The stage with a single generator and no imposed relations. -/
def FinitePresentationStage.single (b : B) : FinitePresentationStage A B :=
  ⟨{b}, ∅, by simp⟩

/-- The stage with the prescribed generators and one prescribed relation. -/
def FinitePresentationStage.ofRel (s : Finset B) (r : MvPolynomial {x : B // x ∈ s} A)
    (hr : MvPolynomial.aeval (fun x : {x : B // x ∈ s} => (x : B)) r = 0) :
    FinitePresentationStage A B :=
  ⟨s, {r}, by simpa using hr⟩

/-- Two polynomials whose difference is an imposed relation of a stage have the same image in
the stage algebra. -/
lemma FinitePresentationStage.mk_eq_of_sub_mem_rels (k : FinitePresentationStage A B)
    {p q : MvPolynomial {x : B // x ∈ k.gens} A} (h : p - q ∈ k.rels) :
    Ideal.Quotient.mk k.rel p = Ideal.Quotient.mk k.rel q := by
  rw [← sub_eq_zero, ← map_sub]
  exact Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.2 (k.rels_le_rel h)

/-- The map out of `B` determined by a cocone on `finitePresentationDiagram`: an element of `B`
is sent through the stage that has it as its only generator. -/
noncomputable def finitePresentationDescFun (T : Cocone (finitePresentationDiagram A B))
    (b : B) : T.pt :=
  finitePresentationLeg T (FinitePresentationStage.single (A := A) b)
    (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (MvPolynomial.X ⟨b, Finset.mem_singleton_self b⟩))

/-- The value of `finitePresentationDescFun` may be computed at any stage having the element as
a generator. -/
lemma finitePresentationDescFun_eq (T : Cocone (finitePresentationDiagram A B))
    (i : FinitePresentationStage A B) {b : B} (hb : b ∈ i.gens) :
    finitePresentationDescFun T b =
      finitePresentationLeg T i (Ideal.Quotient.mk i.rel (MvPolynomial.X ⟨b, hb⟩)) :=
  finitePresentationLeg_X T _ hb

/-- On the image of `A`, `finitePresentationDescFun` is computed by the constants at any
stage. -/
lemma finitePresentationDescFun_algebraMap (T : Cocone (finitePresentationDiagram A B))
    (i : FinitePresentationStage A B) (a : A) :
    finitePresentationDescFun T (algebraMap A B a) =
      finitePresentationLeg T i (Ideal.Quotient.mk i.rel (MvPolynomial.C a)) := by
  have hmem : algebraMap A B a ∈ ({algebraMap A B a} : Finset B) := Finset.mem_singleton_self _
  have hr : MvPolynomial.aeval
      (fun x : {x : B // x ∈ ({algebraMap A B a} : Finset B)} => (x : B))
      ((MvPolynomial.X ⟨algebraMap A B a, hmem⟩ - MvPolynomial.C a :
        MvPolynomial {x : B // x ∈ ({algebraMap A B a} : Finset B)} A)) = 0 := by
    simp only [map_sub, MvPolynomial.aeval_X, MvPolynomial.aeval_C, sub_self]
  have hmem' : algebraMap A B a ∈ (FinitePresentationStage.ofRel _ _ hr).gens := hmem
  have h0 : Ideal.Quotient.mk (FinitePresentationStage.ofRel _ _ hr).rel
        (MvPolynomial.X ⟨algebraMap A B a, hmem'⟩) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk (FinitePresentationStage.ofRel _ _ hr).rel (MvPolynomial.C a) :=
    FinitePresentationStage.mk_eq_of_sub_mem_rels _ (Finset.mem_singleton_self _)
  rw [finitePresentationDescFun_eq T _ hmem', h0]
  exact finitePresentationLeg_C T _ i a

/-- The map out of `B` determined by a cocone on `finitePresentationDiagram`, as a ring map.
Each ring-hom law is read off from a single stage carrying the corresponding relation. -/
noncomputable def finitePresentationDesc (T : Cocone (finitePresentationDiagram A B)) :
    B →+* T.pt where
  toFun := finitePresentationDescFun T
  map_one' := by
    rw [show (1 : B) = algebraMap A B 1 from (map_one (algebraMap A B)).symm,
      finitePresentationDescFun_algebraMap T (FinitePresentationStage.single (A := A) (1 : B)),
      map_one, map_one, map_one]
  map_zero' := by
    rw [show (0 : B) = algebraMap A B 0 from (map_zero (algebraMap A B)).symm,
      finitePresentationDescFun_algebraMap T (FinitePresentationStage.single (A := A) (0 : B)),
      map_zero, map_zero, map_zero]
  map_add' a b := by
    classical
    have ha : a ∈ ({a, b, a + b} : Finset B) := by simp
    have hb : b ∈ ({a, b, a + b} : Finset B) := by simp
    have hab : a + b ∈ ({a, b, a + b} : Finset B) := by simp
    have hr : MvPolynomial.aeval (fun x : {x : B // x ∈ ({a, b, a + b} : Finset B)} => (x : B))
        ((MvPolynomial.X ⟨a + b, hab⟩ -
            (MvPolynomial.X ⟨a, ha⟩ + MvPolynomial.X ⟨b, hb⟩) :
          MvPolynomial {x : B // x ∈ ({a, b, a + b} : Finset B)} A)) = 0 := by
      simp only [map_sub, map_add, MvPolynomial.aeval_X]
      ring
    have ha' : a ∈ (FinitePresentationStage.ofRel _ _ hr).gens := ha
    have hb' : b ∈ (FinitePresentationStage.ofRel _ _ hr).gens := hb
    have hab' : a + b ∈ (FinitePresentationStage.ofRel _ _ hr).gens := hab
    have h0 : Ideal.Quotient.mk (FinitePresentationStage.ofRel _ _ hr).rel
          (MvPolynomial.X ⟨a + b, hab'⟩) =
        Ideal.Quotient.mk (FinitePresentationStage.ofRel _ _ hr).rel
          (MvPolynomial.X ⟨a, ha'⟩ + MvPolynomial.X ⟨b, hb'⟩) :=
      FinitePresentationStage.mk_eq_of_sub_mem_rels _ (Finset.mem_singleton_self _)
    rw [finitePresentationDescFun_eq T _ hab', finitePresentationDescFun_eq T _ ha',
      finitePresentationDescFun_eq T _ hb', h0, map_add, map_add]
  map_mul' a b := by
    classical
    have ha : a ∈ ({a, b, a * b} : Finset B) := by simp
    have hb : b ∈ ({a, b, a * b} : Finset B) := by simp
    have hab : a * b ∈ ({a, b, a * b} : Finset B) := by simp
    have hr : MvPolynomial.aeval (fun x : {x : B // x ∈ ({a, b, a * b} : Finset B)} => (x : B))
        ((MvPolynomial.X ⟨a * b, hab⟩ -
            MvPolynomial.X ⟨a, ha⟩ * MvPolynomial.X ⟨b, hb⟩ :
          MvPolynomial {x : B // x ∈ ({a, b, a * b} : Finset B)} A)) = 0 := by
      simp only [map_sub, map_mul, MvPolynomial.aeval_X]
      ring
    have ha' : a ∈ (FinitePresentationStage.ofRel _ _ hr).gens := ha
    have hb' : b ∈ (FinitePresentationStage.ofRel _ _ hr).gens := hb
    have hab' : a * b ∈ (FinitePresentationStage.ofRel _ _ hr).gens := hab
    have h0 : Ideal.Quotient.mk (FinitePresentationStage.ofRel _ _ hr).rel
          (MvPolynomial.X ⟨a * b, hab'⟩) =
        Ideal.Quotient.mk (FinitePresentationStage.ofRel _ _ hr).rel
          (MvPolynomial.X ⟨a, ha'⟩ * MvPolynomial.X ⟨b, hb'⟩) :=
      FinitePresentationStage.mk_eq_of_sub_mem_rels _ (Finset.mem_singleton_self _)
    rw [finitePresentationDescFun_eq T _ hab', finitePresentationDescFun_eq T _ ha',
      finitePresentationDescFun_eq T _ hb', h0, map_mul, map_mul]

/-- Evaluation at the generators exhibits `B` as the colimit of the system of its finite,
finitely presented approximations.  This is the affine form of [Stacks, Tag 0817] (2). -/
noncomputable def finitePresentationIsColimit :
    IsColimit (finitePresentationCocone A B) where
  desc T := CommRingCat.ofHom (finitePresentationDesc T)
  fac T i := by
    have key : ((finitePresentationDesc T).comp i.evalHom.toRingHom) =
        (finitePresentationLeg T i).comp (Ideal.Quotient.mk i.rel) := by
      refine MvPolynomial.ringHom_ext (fun a => ?_) (fun x => ?_)
      · change finitePresentationDescFun T (i.evalHom (MvPolynomial.C a)) =
          finitePresentationLeg T i (Ideal.Quotient.mk i.rel (MvPolynomial.C a))
        rw [FinitePresentationStage.evalHom_C]
        exact finitePresentationDescFun_algebraMap T i a
      · change finitePresentationDescFun T (i.evalHom (MvPolynomial.X x)) =
          finitePresentationLeg T i (Ideal.Quotient.mk i.rel (MvPolynomial.X x))
        rw [FinitePresentationStage.evalHom_X]
        exact finitePresentationDescFun_eq T i x.2
    refine CommRingCat.hom_ext (RingHom.ext fun x => ?_)
    obtain ⟨w, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective x
    exact RingHom.congr_fun key w
  uniq T m hm := by
    have key : ∀ b : B, m.hom b = finitePresentationDescFun T b := by
      intro b
      have h := hm (FinitePresentationStage.single (A := A) b)
      calc m.hom b
          = m.hom ((FinitePresentationStage.single (A := A) b).evalHom
              (MvPolynomial.X ⟨b, Finset.mem_singleton_self b⟩)) := by
            rw [FinitePresentationStage.evalHom_X]
        _ = finitePresentationLeg T (FinitePresentationStage.single (A := A) b)
              (Ideal.Quotient.mk _
                (MvPolynomial.X ⟨b, Finset.mem_singleton_self b⟩)) :=
            congrArg
              (fun φ : (finitePresentationDiagram A B).obj
                  (FinitePresentationStage.single (A := A) b) ⟶ T.pt =>
                φ.hom (Ideal.Quotient.mk _
                  (MvPolynomial.X ⟨b, Finset.mem_singleton_self b⟩))) h
        _ = finitePresentationDescFun T b := rfl
    exact CommRingCat.hom_ext (RingHom.ext fun b => key b)

variable (A B)

/-- The structure morphisms to `Spec A` of the inverse system of spectra of the finite, finitely
presented approximations of `B`. -/
noncomputable def finitePresentationSpecStructureMap :
    (finitePresentationDiagram A B).op ⋙ Scheme.Spec ⟶
      (Functor.const (FinitePresentationStage A B)ᵒᵖ).obj (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)) where
  app i := Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A i.unop.ring))
  naturality i j h := by
    have key : CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A j.unop.ring) ≫
        (finitePresentationDiagram A B).map h.unop =
          CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A i.unop.ring) := by
      ext a
      exact (FinitePresentationStage.map (leOfHom h.unop)).commutes a
    change Spec.map ((finitePresentationDiagram A B).map h.unop) ≫
        Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A j.unop.ring)) =
      Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A i.unop.ring)) ≫ 𝟙 _
    rw [Category.comp_id]
    exact (Spec.map_comp _ _).symm.trans (congrArg Spec.map key)

/-- For an integral algebra `B` over `A`, the spectrum of `B` is the directed inverse limit of
the spectra of the finite, finitely presented approximations of `B`, each of which is finite and
of finite presentation over `Spec A`.

This is the affine-target case of [Stacks, Tag 09YZ]. -/
noncomputable def finitePresentationLimitPresentationSpec :
    FinitePresentationLimitPresentation
      (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))) where
  indexType := FinitePresentationStage A B
  diagram := (finitePresentationDiagram A B).op ⋙ Scheme.Spec
  structureMap := finitePresentationSpecStructureMap A B
  limitCone := (Scheme.Spec.mapCone (finitePresentationCocone A B).op).π
  compatible i := by
    have key : CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A i.unop.ring) ≫
        (finitePresentationCocone A B).ι.app i.unop =
          CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B) := by
      ext a
      exact i.unop.toB.commutes a
    change Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B)) =
      Spec.map ((finitePresentationCocone A B).ι.app i.unop) ≫
        Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A i.unop.ring))
    exact (congrArg Spec.map key).symm.trans (Spec.map_comp _ _)
  isLimit :=
    isLimitOfPreserves Scheme.Spec (finitePresentationIsColimit (A := A) (B := B)).op
  stageFinite i := by
    refine (AlgebraicGeometry.IsFinite.SpecMap_iff
      (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A i.unop.ring))).mpr ?_
    exact RingHom.finite_algebraMap.mpr (FinitePresentationStage.moduleFinite i.unop)
  stageLocallyOfFinitePresentation i := by
    refine (AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyOfFinitePresentation.SpecMap_iff
      (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A i.unop.ring))).mpr ?_
    exact RingHom.finitePresentation_algebraMap.mpr
      (FinitePresentationStage.finitePresentation i.unop)

end AffineFinitePresentation

/-- An integral morphism of schemes with affine target is the directed inverse limit of a system
of finite morphisms to the same target.

This is the affine-target case of [Stacks, Tag 09YZ] with the weaker conclusion that the stages
are finite. It is deliberately left untagged: the source states the result for a quasi-compact
and quasi-separated target, and asserts in addition that the stages are of finite presentation
over the target. For the stronger conclusion over an affine target see
`finitePresentationLimitPresentation`. -/
noncomputable def integralLimitPresentation {X S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S)
    [IsIntegralHom f] [IsAffine S] : IntegralLimitPresentation f := by
  haveI : IsAffine X := isAffine_of_isAffineHom f
  letI : Algebra Γ(S, ⊤) Γ(X, ⊤) := RingHom.toAlgebra (Scheme.Hom.appTop f).hom
  haveI : Algebra.IsIntegral Γ(S, ⊤) Γ(X, ⊤) :=
    algebraMap_isIntegral_iff.mp
      ((@HasAffineProperty.iff_of_isAffine _ _ IsIntegralHom.hasAffineProperty _ _ f
        inferInstance).mp inferInstance).2
  have hmap : CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap Γ(S, ⊤) Γ(X, ⊤)) = Scheme.Hom.appTop f := rfl
  refine (hmap ▸ integralLimitPresentationSpec Γ(S, ⊤) Γ(X, ⊤)).ofIso X.isoSpec S.isoSpec ?_
  exact (Scheme.isoSpec_hom_naturality f).symm

/-- An integral morphism of schemes with affine target is the directed inverse limit of a system
of morphisms to the same target which are finite and of finite presentation.

This is the affine-target case of [Stacks, Tag 09YZ], with the full conclusion of the source.
It is deliberately left untagged: the source states the result for a quasi-compact and
quasi-separated target, which is not proved here. -/
noncomputable def finitePresentationLimitPresentation {X S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S)
    [IsIntegralHom f] [IsAffine S] : FinitePresentationLimitPresentation f := by
  haveI : IsAffine X := isAffine_of_isAffineHom f
  letI : Algebra Γ(S, ⊤) Γ(X, ⊤) := RingHom.toAlgebra (Scheme.Hom.appTop f).hom
  haveI : Algebra.IsIntegral Γ(S, ⊤) Γ(X, ⊤) :=
    algebraMap_isIntegral_iff.mp
      ((@HasAffineProperty.iff_of_isAffine _ _ IsIntegralHom.hasAffineProperty _ _ f
        inferInstance).mp inferInstance).2
  have hmap : CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap Γ(S, ⊤) Γ(X, ⊤)) = Scheme.Hom.appTop f := rfl
  refine (hmap ▸ finitePresentationLimitPresentationSpec Γ(S, ⊤) Γ(X, ⊤)).ofIso
    X.isoSpec S.isoSpec ?_
  exact (Scheme.isoSpec_hom_naturality f).symm

end Stacks.EtaleCohomology

